Boot splash artwork (rootfs/splash/)

tsx-linux-mark.svg
    The TSX-LINUX word mark. This project's own artwork, GPL-2.0-or-later
    like the rest of the repository. The text is set in JetBrains Mono
    Bold (see below).

tux-80.png
    Tux, the Linux penguin, by Larry Ewing <lewing@isc.tamu.edu>, drawn
    with The GIMP. This is the Linux kernel's own boot logo,
    drivers/video/logo/logo_linux_clut224.ppm (80x80, 224 colours;
    "Copyright (C) 1996 Larry Ewing" in drivers/video/logo/logo.c),
    GPL-2.0 like the kernel, converted losslessly from PPM to PNG. Larry
    Ewing's permission note: "Permission to use and/or modify this image is
    granted provided you acknowledge me lewing@isc.tamu.edu and The GIMP if
    someone asks."

Fonts (not in the repository; installed from Alpine packages in the build
container by mksplash.sh, rendered into the splash images at build time):
    JetBrains Mono Bold (font-jetbrains-mono), Copyright 2020 The JetBrains
    Mono Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1: the word mark.
    Terminus (font-terminus: ter-116n, ter-124n), Copyright Dimitar Toshkov
    Zhekov, SIL Open Font License 1.1: the status line.
    Terminus bold console fonts (font-terminus: ter-116b ... ter-132b, same
    copyright and licence), copied into the initramfs by
    rootfs/initramfs/mkinitramfs-switchroot.sh: the text console font
    (tsx-confont).

The rescue status screen and /etc/motd use the classic public-domain ASCII
Tux (seven lines, "|o_o |") next to "TSX - LINUX" in figlet's smslant font.
